  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contracting in Illinois through FY2027 to date shows concentrated spending and a large number of small awards. Total obligations in Illinois are $724M across 29,184 awards, with an average award size of $24.8K and obligations down 94.5% year over year. Obligations for prior full fiscal years ranged from $13B to $14.4B, with FY22 at $13.7B, FY23 at $13.5B, FY24 at $14.4B, FY25 at $13B, and FY26 at $13.3B. The Department of Energy and the Department of Veterans Affairs are the top buyers so far in FY2027 to date, obligating $297M and $264M respectively. FERMI FORWARD DISCOVERY GROUP, LLC and UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC are the largest vendors to date, receiving $173M and $124M respectively. Research and development activities lead industries by obligation, with Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $175M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $124M. Medical supply wholesalers are also significant, with Medical, Dental, and Hospital Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers at $91.2M.",
    "sections": [
